<title>PORTUGAL: Share trade halted in Banco Totta, Sotto.</title>
<headline>Share trade halted in Banco Totta, Sotto.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Financial Markets Committee (CMVM) suspended share trade in Banco Totta &amp; Acores and Banco Pinto &amp; Sotto Mayor, dealers said.</p>
<p>Both banks are controlled by the Champalimaud group. Share trade in the group's financial holding and insurer Mundial Confianca was not halted, the dealers added.  </p>
<p>The suspensions followed newspaper reports on Friday that the Champalimaud group was planning to merge the two banks by launching a public offer to buy shares in Banco Totta not held by the group.</p>
<p>Officials at the CMVM were not immediately available to comment on the suspension.</p>
<p>Champalimaud group officials were also not available.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
